wireguard: queueing: always return valid online CPU in wg_cpumask_choose_online()

Mainline commit 5bd8de20770c (Linux 6.18), applied to amneziawg's copy of queueing.h, which
the amneziawg tree does not carry yet.

A CPU going offline between num_online_cpus() and cpumask_nth() makes cpumask_nth() return
nr_cpu_ids or more. queue_work_on() only rejects WORK_CPU_UNBOUND (NR_CPUS), so the bogus CPU
reaches per-CPU data. Retrying until the CPU is online closes the window.

--- a/src/queueing.h
+++ b/src/queueing.h
@@ -115,7 +115,7 @@
 {
 	unsigned int cpu = *stored_cpu;
 
-	if (unlikely(cpu >= nr_cpu_ids || !cpu_online(cpu)))
+	while (unlikely(cpu >= nr_cpu_ids || !cpu_online(cpu)))
 		cpu = *stored_cpu = cpumask_nth(id % num_online_cpus(), cpu_online_mask);
 
 	return cpu;
